cal and empirical performance persists, even in minimal, easily analysable setups. This suggests a fundamental problem. As proof that larger capacities are indeed possible, we train Chunky Seal, a scaled-up version of Video Seal, which increases capacity 4× to 1024 bits , all while preserving image quality and robustness.\nL48: These findings demonstrate modern methods have not yet saturated watermarking capacity, and that significant opportunities for architectural innovation and training strategies remain.\nL49: cite18†Download the Paper†scontent-hkg1-2.xx.fbcdn.net L50: #### AUTHORS\nL51: \nL52: Written by\nL53: \nL54: Aleksandar Petrov\nL55: \nL56: Pierre Fernandez\nL57: \nL58: Tomáš Souček\nL59: \nL60: Hady Elsahar\nL61: \nL62: Publisher\nL63: \nL64: arxiv\nL65: \nL66: Research Topics\nL67: \nL68: cite19†Computer Vision L69: \nL70: ### Related Publications\nL71: \nL72: August 04, 2026\nL73: \nL74: #### COMPUTER VISION\nL75: \nL76: #### WaiT for the Signal: Simple Frequency-Aware Flow-Matching\nL77: \nL78: Krunoslav Lehman Pavasovic, Theophane Vallaeys, Stéphane Mallat, Giulio Biroli, cite20†Luke Zettlemoyer , Brian Karrer, Jakob Verbeek\nL79: \nL80: August 04, 2026\nL81: \nL82: cite21†Read the Paper L83: \nL84: July 13, 2026\nL85: \nL86: #### AR/VR\nL87: \nL88: #### RESEARCH\nL89: #### S-EMBER: A Large-Scale Benchmark for Streaming Egocentric Memory Retrieval\nL90: \nL91: Xiaodong Wang, Xuanyi Zhao, cite22†Pedro Rodriguez , Devendra Singh Sachan, cite23†Barlas Oguz , Seungwhan Moon, cite24†Shang-Wen Li , Gargi Ghosh, Xin Dong, cite25†Wen-Tau Yih L92: \nL93: July 13, 2026\nL94: \nL95: cite26†Read the Paper L96: \nL97: July 03, 2026\nL98: \nL99: #### HUMAN & MACHINE INTELLIGENCE\nL100: \nL101: #### ROBOTICS\nL102: #### Interpreting Physics in Video World Models\nL103: \nL104: Sonia Joseph, Quentin Garrido, Randall Balestriero, Matthew Kowal, Thomas Fel, Shahab Bakhtiari, Blake Richards, Mike Rabbat\nL105: \nL106: July 03, 2026\nL107: \n